{"content_hash": "268cb8bb506fe7fd", "version_id": 572, "article_id": 58, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Nikon takes back prize after AI image wins", "title_zh": "尼康收回奖项，因为获奖图片是AI做的", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "bbc_tech", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr86z33pdy9vo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614036417651-efe5912149d8?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cHJpemUlMjB3aW5uaW5nJTIwaW1hZ2V8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MTc2NTYxNXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brands&People on Unsplash", "author": "Brands&People", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brandsandpeople?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/yellow-paper-award-ribbon-ZdqSuxl3Lak?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(16, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(54, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "cec84960fed8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 150, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "A photo contest winner lost his prize. Nikon says the picture was made with AI, and that is against the rules.", "lead_zh": "一位摄影比赛的获奖者被取消了奖项。尼康说这张图片是用AI做的，这违反了比赛规则。", "preview": "Nikon runs a famous science photo contest. It started 15 years ago. The contest is for very small things seen with microscopes. On 9 October", "preview_zh": "尼康举办一个很有名的科学摄影比赛。这个比赛15年前开始。比赛拍的是显微镜下非常小的东西。2026年10月9日，尼康说一位获奖者用AI做了视频。所以他被取消了奖项。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 561, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/58/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 62.812, "size_bytes": 380592, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 169, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@4cb6f94/content/data/versions/572.json", "paragraphs": ["Nikon runs a famous science photo contest. It started 15 years ago. The contest is for very small things seen with microscopes. On 9 October 2026, Nikon said one winner used AI to make his video. So he lost the prize.", "The winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hairs moving in a child's airway. The child has a lung illness called PCD. Xu said he used AI, but he thought it was allowed.", "Many scientists did not believe the video was real. Dr Robert Hirst studies PCD in England. He said the cells did not look like real PCD cells. He has checked PCD cells for 20 years. He was not surprised.", "Nikon said it will look at its contest rules again. The company said it was not judging Xu as a person. Many patients and doctors were upset by this problem."], "paragraphs_zh": ["尼康举办一个很有名的科学摄影比赛。这个比赛15年前开始。比赛拍的是显微镜下非常小的东西。2026年10月9日，尼康说一位获奖者用AI做了视频。所以他被取消了奖项。", "获奖者是来自中国清华大学的徐宁博士。他的视频显示一个孩子气道里细小的毛在动。这个孩子得了一种叫PCD的肺病。徐宁说他用了AI，但他以为这是允许的。", "很多科学家不相信这个视频是真的。罗伯特·赫斯特博士在英国研究PCD。他说这些细胞不像真的PCD细胞。他检查PCD细胞已经20年了。他并不惊讶。", "尼康说会重新看看比赛规则。公司说这不是在评价徐宁这个人。很多病人和医生因为这件事很难过。"], "body": "Nikon runs a famous science photo contest. It started 15 years ago. The contest is for very small things seen with microscopes. On 9 October 2026, Nikon said one winner used AI to make his video. So he lost the prize.\n\nThe winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hairs moving in a child's airway. The child has a lung illness called PCD. Xu said he used AI, but he thought it was allowed.\n\nMany scientists did not believe the video was real. Dr Robert Hirst studies PCD in England. He said the cells did not look like real PCD cells. He has checked PCD cells for 20 years. He was not surprised.\n\nNikon said it will look at its contest rules again. The company said it was not judging Xu as a person. Many patients and doctors were upset by this problem.", "body_zh": "尼康举办一个很有名的科学摄影比赛。这个比赛15年前开始。比赛拍的是显微镜下非常小的东西。2026年10月9日，尼康说一位获奖者用AI做了视频。所以他被取消了奖项。\n\n获奖者是来自中国清华大学的徐宁博士。他的视频显示一个孩子气道里细小的毛在动。这个孩子得了一种叫PCD的肺病。徐宁说他用了AI，但他以为这是允许的。\n\n很多科学家不相信这个视频是真的。罗伯特·赫斯特博士在英国研究PCD。他说这些细胞不像真的PCD细胞。他检查PCD细胞已经20年了。他并不惊讶。\n\n尼康说会重新看看比赛规则。公司说这不是在评价徐宁这个人。很多病人和医生因为这件事很难过。", "text": "Nikon runs a famous science photo contest. It started 15 years ago. The contest is for very small things seen with microscopes. On 9 October 2026, Nikon said one winner used AI to make his video. So he lost the prize. The winner was Dr Ning Xu from Tsinghua University in China. His video showed tiny hairs moving in a child's airway. The child has a lung illness called PCD. Xu said he used AI, but he thought it was allowed. Many scientists did not believe the video was real. Dr Robert Hirst studies PCD in England. He said the cells did not look like real PCD cells. He has checked PCD cells for 20 years. He was not surprised. Nikon said it will look at its contest rules again. The company said it was not judging Xu as a person. Many patients and doctors were upset by this problem.", "vocab": [{"word": "contest", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比赛", "note": "常指有奖品的比赛", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "prize", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奖品；奖项", "note": "win a prize 获奖", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rule", "pos": "noun", "zh": "规则", "note": "break the rules 违反规则", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "winner", "pos": "noun", "zh": "获胜者", "note": "来自 win", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "video", "pos": "noun", "zh": "视频", "note": "make a video 拍视频", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "microscope", "pos": "noun", "zh": "显微镜", "note": "看很小的东西用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "scientist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "科学家", "note": "研究科学的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "disqualify", "pos": "verb", "zh": "取消资格", "note": "常用被动 be disqualified", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules", "summary_original": "The camera-maker says it is now re-evaluating the rules and procedures of its Small World in Motion contest.", "body_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules\nBy\nZoe Kleinman\nTechnology & AI editor\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nThe winner of a prestigious scientific photography competition has been disqualified following concerns raised by other scientists that it was fake.\nNikon said the use of generative AI in the composition of the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which accepts photos and video taken using powerful microscopes.\nThe firm said the video \"did not comply with the competition rules regarding generative AI\", but added it was not a judgement of the entrant's professional reputation or scientific contributions.\nIt said it would now look at the rules and procedures of the annual contest, which has been running for 15 years and is specifically for microscopic images.\nNikon said it came to the decision \"after thoroughly re-evaluating the video and supporting materials and consulting with members of our judging panel\".\nThe winning entry came from Dr Ning Xu, from Tsinghua University in China, who submitted a short video showing tiny, hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD.\nThe BBC has approached him for comment.\nA number of scientists, including former competition judges, complained to Nikon on its LinkedIn page that the video did not appear to be real.\nXu had acknowledged using AI, but said he believed he had acted within the rules, and had cooperated with Nikon's investigation.\nUniversity of Leicester scientist Dr Robert Hirst, who was among the first experts to voice concerns, said he was \"not surprised\" and he \"knew immediately that the video was fabricated\".\n\"I have been diagnosing PCD for 20 years by examining their cilia waveform, length, cell size and shape,\" he said.\nHirst, who is lead scientist for the NHS centre for PCD diagnosis at the university, said the cells and cilia \"look nothing like those from PCD patients\".\n\"This controversy has impacted a lot of patients, scientists, doctors and PCD support networks around the world,\" he said.\nTiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon photo contest\nPublished\n1 October\nWhat is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?\nPublished\n14 September\nSign up for our Tech Decoded newsletter\nto follow the world's top tech stories and trends.\nOutside the UK? Sign up here\n.\nRelated topics\nArtificial intelligence\nPhotography\nScience & Environment", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:40:13.616651", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Nikon", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.688, "sm": 100, "em": 687, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "runs", "s": 0.7, "e": 0.925, "sm": 700, "em": 924, "cs": 6, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "a", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.012, "sm": 937, "em": 1012, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "famous", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.412, "sm": 1025, "em": 1412, "cs": 13, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "science", "s": 1.425, "e": 1.825, "sm": 1425, "em": 1825, "cs": 20, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "photo", "s": 1.837, "e": 2.087, "sm": 1837, "em": 2087, "cs": 28, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "contest", "s": 2.1, "e": 2.862, "sm": 2100, "em": 2862, "cs": 34, "ce": 41, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": ".", "s": 2.862, "e": 3.725, "sm": 2862, "em": 3725, "cs": 41, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "It", "s": 3.725, "e": 3.925, "sm": 3725, "em": 3925, "cs": 43, "ce": 45, "si": 1}, {"i": 9, "w": "started", "s": 3.938, "e": 4.362, "sm": 3937, "em": 4362, "cs": 46, "ce": 53, "si": 1}, {"i": 10, "w": "15", "s": 4.375, "e": 4.589, "sm": 4375, "em": 4589, "cs": 54, "ce": 56, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "years", "s": 4.589, "e": 5.125, "sm": 4589, "em": 5125, "cs": 57, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": "ago", "s": 5.138, "e": 5.55, "sm": 5137, "em": 5550, "cs": 63, "ce": 66, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": ".", "s": 5.55, "e": 6.425, "sm": 5550, "em": 6425, "cs": 66